ci(security): gate CodeQL on file coverage, drop the temporary probe

Two things the real Security runs corrected. The Go extraction-error
diagnostics carry no location at all, so the source-root split the first
commit gated on could never fire. And the failures were not unannotated: the
runner already raises nine failure-level check-run annotations for them, but
untitled, at paths it mis-parsed out of the log text, under a green check --
unreadable rather than absent, which is what let 55 runs pass unnoticed.

So the gate moves to the coverage sets in the same SARIF -- expected files
against successfully-extracted ones -- which are per-file and source-root
relative. An expected file that never reached the database is this repo's own
code going unanalysed and fails the job; extraction errors warn and stay green.
Excludes _test.go, which `go build` never compiles, and reports rather than
passes when an analysis publishes no baseline, as the actions row does not.

